    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for LawDog today hinges on the favorable matchup against Ryan Feltner, providing elite utility for **Luis Arraez** (66.77) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.64). **Lawrence Butler** stands out as the day\u2019s top play (73.46) as he faces Tyler Phillips in a park conducive to his power-speed profile, benefitting from a massive +13% platoon adjustment. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** (68.45) is a primary start at 1B; his high xwOBA and prime spot in the two-hole against Arrighetti make him a foundational piece of today's production stack. While **Daulton Varsho** (60.75) faces a stiff test against Luis Castillo, his dynamic platoon advantage remains high enough to warrant a strong start, even against a tough arm.\n\nThe most challenging decision for the bench was **Gavin Sheets** (44.21), who fell short of the threshold due to an unfavorable matchup against Shohei Ohtani. While his underlying metrics are decent, the lack of a confirmed lineup position and the elite nature of the opposing pitcher suppressed his efficiency score below the starting threshold. Elsewhere, we are navigating minor risks with several \"Lineup Pending\" designations; **Cal Raleigh** (41.82) is of particular concern, as his score is heavily pressured by a -19% penalty against the formidable Dylan Cease. We also continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Bryson Stott**, who remain unavailable due to injury or scheduling, further tightening the roster's flexibility. Managers should track final lineups for **Cal Raleigh**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Lawrence Butler** to ensure projected spots hold firm against these high-leverage starters.",
